 "why": "CORRECTED 2026-08-26. An earlier revision of this field said the factor-one rows are 'the default build at the committed budget', which is false for most of these arms: the adapter compiles them with -DAMP=1, overriding each pair's compiled-in default, so where a pair's AMP is in a source the arm compiles the second acquisition is a rebuild at a different gain. Only the division pair's two arms and the patched arms of the two ECDSA pairs are the same binary, and same_binary records which.",
